  // Discovery — the enrollment window, and the quarantine that makes it safe to open.
  'disc.model.title': 'How a new device gets in',
  'disc.model.p1': 'A device that is not in the inventory cannot connect to the broker at all. That is the security model: the device list IS the credential store, which is why deleting a device really revokes it.',
  'disc.model.p2': 'But nobody onboards two hundred door contacts by typing two hundred device keys. So you open a door on purpose: an enrollment window mints a one-time key, and it closes itself when the time runs out.',
  'disc.model.p3': 'Anything that walks through it is QUARANTINED. What it publishes becomes a candidate below and nothing else — no telemetry is stored for it and no rule is evaluated. Someone who slips into the window can leave junk for you to decline; they cannot forge a reading, move a chart, or trigger or suppress an alert.',
