  'wiz.what.title': 'What this app does',
  'wiz.what.body': 'It listens to what your sensors publish over MQTT, records the readings that actually changed, watches them with rules you write, and tells you when something is wrong — a freezer warming up, a door opening at 03:00, a sensor that has gone quiet.',
  'wiz.what.empty': 'There are no devices yet, so there is nothing to chart and nothing to alert on. The empty pages are honest, not broken.',
  'wiz.enrol.title': 'How your first device gets in',
  'wiz.enrol.body': 'A device that is not in the inventory cannot connect to the broker at all. To onboard one you open a time-boxed enrollment window, which mints a one-time key — shown once — that you flash into the device as its broker password.',
  'wiz.enrol.quarantine': 'Devices that present the key are admitted but quarantined: what they publish becomes a candidate for you to review, and nothing else. No telemetry is stored for them and no rule is evaluated, so nothing that walks through the window is trusted until you adopt it.',
  'wiz.ready.title': 'That is the whole path',
  'wiz.ready.body': 'Nothing here has been configured for you and nothing is running yet. When you are ready:',
  'wiz.ready.s1': 'Open an enrollment window on the Discovery page and copy the key.',
  'wiz.ready.s2': 'Point your first device at this hub with that key, then adopt it from the candidate list — the hub will suggest what it is from the fields it publishes, and adopting it mints its real, permanent credential.',
  'wiz.ready.s3': 'Give it a device type so its readings can be decoded, then write a rule so it can tell you something.',
